This project contains modified source code and data derived from
KrisCris/Palworld-Pal-Editor, which was distributed under GPL-3.0:
https://github.com/KrisCris/Palworld-Pal-Editor

The import baseline also includes Palworld 1.0 compatibility work from
RayChen200318/Palworld-Pal-Editor-1.0 at commit
ce5ff571ff34cca536bb13f398d9bd53420760e2:
https://github.com/RayChen200318/Palworld-Pal-Editor-1.0

The offline item catalog uses formal Palworld item metadata from
oMaN-Rod/palworld-save-pal at commit
d8907c4adfd4e9cae471e49b1c4bf5359f89402d, with English and Chinese
display names and item icon references matched from PalDB Items:
https://github.com/oMaN-Rod/palworld-save-pal
https://paldb.cc/en/Items
https://paldb.cc/cn/Items

The resulting catalog and WebP icon bundle are stored locally so the item
manager does not contact those services at runtime. PalDB and the bundled game
artwork remain the property of their respective owners.

The offline Pal, passive-trait, and active-skill catalogs include English and
Chinese display names and game descriptions matched from PalDB's bilingual
reference pages:
https://paldb.cc/en/Passive_Skills
https://paldb.cc/cn/Passive_Skills
https://paldb.cc/en/Active_Skills
https://paldb.cc/cn/Active_Skills

Those descriptions and skill statistics are packaged with the application;
the editor does not contact PalDB at runtime.

